WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.601
-We are joined right now
by a legendary chef.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:05.133
He's an Emmy and James Beard
Award winner

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:07.601
and the founder of
the Jacques Pépin Foundation.

00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:10.501
Everyone please welcome
Chef Jacques Pépin!

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:12.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.434 --> 00:00:14.968
I love you. Come on. I love you!

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:17.868
Welcome back to the show.
I love you.

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:20.434
Tomorrow is Thanksgiving, and I
was just wondering if you could

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:24.234
show me how to properly carve
a turkey because I am a moron.

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:25.868
I have no idea what I'm doing.

00:00:25.868 --> 00:00:27.300
-I'll show you how to carve it.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.300
Properly? I don't know.
-Okay, alright.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.367
But let's see the way
Jacques Pépin does it.

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:33.367
-To start with,
when you roast it like this,

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:35.000
you remove the wishbone.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.100
You know, that triangle here?
-Oh, okay.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.367
-It's in the way to carve,
so you remove it.

00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:41.767
See, they remove it
before cooking. It's here.

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:43.400
And here, you've got to pull on
the other side.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.701
-Let's make a wish.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:45.968
[ Audience ohs ]

00:00:45.968 --> 00:00:48.100
Wow! What happened?

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.534
We both got our wishes
came true. Yeah!

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:53.667
That was cool.

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:55.234
That's so cool. Look at this.

00:00:55.234 --> 00:00:56.667
That just popped off equally.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:58.868
Oh, my gosh. I'm saving this.
Okay, cool.

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:01.701
-So, anyway, so here like this,
you can do that.

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:04.434
So here, now you can cut
this way directly.

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:07.400
And then you go right
down into slice.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.667
[ Audience oohs ]

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.701
-Now, see, this is --
I can't do this.

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:11.834
-Of course you can.

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:13.067
You're going to do
the other side.

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:14.968
-Oh, oh, my gosh.
I actually am going to do this.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:16.667
-Yeah, do this side here.

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:18.234
Or you can do it maybe bigger.

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:20.434
So, you cut it this way.
-Yep. Cut it that way.

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:21.968
Watch out, be careful,
I'm not -- around me.

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:23.367
-Lower.
-Lower?

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:25.334
-Yeah, that's it.
-Right under the wishbone thing?

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:26.934
-Yes.
-Go across.

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:28.300
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:29.634
-Yeah, yeah, beautiful.

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:31.434
-Wow, that felt good.
-That's how you start slicing.

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:32.801
-And then slice it like this?

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:35.734
-Yes. Now you go -- Because now
it stops right there.

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:36.801
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:40.100
-Whoa, you're good.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Look at this.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.067
Whoa, look at this!
-Perfect.

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:44.801
-Are you kidding me?
I'm gonna stop here

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:46.467
just 'cause it looks so good.
-Yeah, that's perfect.

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:51.167
Then we remove the dark meat,
you know?

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:53.767
Dark meat. I use my hand.
It's easier.

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:55.767
-Yeah. Of course, you just get
right in there

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.100
and remove it with your hand.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:03.367
-And you take the drumstick
and you cut it in half.

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.934
And then, now we cut that
in two pieces.

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:10.234
Make sure to use the skin
because the skin is very good.

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:11.968
-The skin is the best.
-Do you want to taste it?

00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:13.667
-I do. I would love to taste it.
Sure.

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:16.968
Oh, my gosh.

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:18.567
I love just doing
anything with you.

00:02:18.567 --> 00:02:19.901
Yeah, that was amazing.

00:02:19.901 --> 00:02:21.534
I wanted to ask you something.

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:25.200
My favorite part is the next
day, or maybe even later

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.801
that night when you make
a turkey sandwich.

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:28.033
-Oh, yes.
[ Cheers ]

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:29.234
-You know what I'm saying?
-I love turkey sandwich.

00:02:29.234 --> 00:02:31.000
-You do?
I was thinking what we could do

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.467
is maybe make a sandwich
and give Questlove --

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:35.234
You can be our taste tester.
-Okay.

00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:37.067
-And then he can say who made

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:39.100
the better Thanksgiving
sandwich.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.934
You want to have a competition?

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:42.400
-Fine.
-You ready for this?

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:45.901
Now, before we start,

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:49.100
we need Quest to put on
the dome of silence

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.200
so he won't know
who made which --

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:54.834
Alright, so, can you --
You can't see, right?

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:56.868
Okay, perfect.
Ready to make this sandwich?

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:58.334
He can't hear anything either.

00:02:58.334 --> 00:02:59.901
-I can take any bread I want?

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:01.567
Here, okay, here.
-You're doing that bread?

00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:05.467
-Yes. I have some stuff
underneath here.

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:06.667
-You have a secret ingredient?

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:09.334
-Yeah, I have some sriracha,
some hot sauce.

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:10.901
-Sriracha?
-Yes.

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:13.100
-Alright.
-You want some of it?

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.434
-No.
-Oh, good.

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:15.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:17.200
-I think I'm going stuffing
all the way.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.534
I really think stuffing
is a big hit this year.

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:21.167
-Some mustard here.
-Mustard? Okay.

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.234
Sriracha and mustard.
I'm just going stuffing.

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:24.734
This is going to be real dry
though, right?

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:25.934
-I have some olive oil.

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:28.000
-What are you doing?
Oh, olive oil.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.567
Oh, yeah, I might use some of
that olive oil.

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:30.801
-I have some lettuce too.

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:32.267
-Lettuce is delicious,
but, you know.

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:34.300
-Want some lettuce?
-No.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.667
Yeah, it looks nice, right?
Yeah.

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:36.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:38.133
Alright, lettuce is good.

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:39.834
I'll put one -- two things of
lettuce on there.

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:40.868
Ooh, look at that.

00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:41.901
It's actually gonna be good.

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:44.200
I'm going to do a little gravy
on mine.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:47.467
Should I put it on the bread
so the breads --

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:49.267
kind of sops it up a little bit?

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:50.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:52.067
-Can I have some gravy too?

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:53.701
-Yeah, I guess so.
-Okay.

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:56.067
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, you can have some gravy.

00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:57.634
Alright, so you're putting gravy
too.

00:03:57.634 --> 00:04:00.634
How is Questlove drumming
while not seeing or hearing?

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:01.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:03.968
Alright. Turkey right here.

00:04:03.968 --> 00:04:06.067
And then --
-You took the piece I wanted.

00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:08.234
-I know I did, right?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:10.400
I took the good one, right?
I carved that side.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.767
-No, no, I'm doing
only the dark meat.

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:14.501
-I think Quest would think --
-I like the dark meat.

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:16.033
-What is this? What's that?

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:19.100
-Oh, this is the gratin
that my mother used to do.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:23.467
In France, we never do --
we never do sweet pumpkin.

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:25.734
The pumpkin is done with
cream and cheese.

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:27.067
You want to taste it?

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:28.634
-Yeah, I do want to taste it,
to just check it out.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.234
Sorry.

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:31.200
Oh, my gosh.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.267
-Want to put it
in your sandwich?

00:04:32.267 --> 00:04:33.734
-Yeah, that's --
I want that recipe.

00:04:33.734 --> 00:04:37.133
The gratin.
Ooh, Jacques Pépin gratin.

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:38.634
Here we go.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.634 --> 00:04:40.100
Alright, gonna put
a little cranberry.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.400
Just a little --
just a little bit.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.634
Just enough. Just enough.

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:44.534
And then look at this.

00:04:44.534 --> 00:04:45.667
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:47.133
-Wow.

00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:48.434
That's sugar, though.

00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:49.634
-Oh, wait, it's not sugar,
is it?

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:54.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:56.934
You got me, buddy. Oh, my gosh.

00:04:56.934 --> 00:04:58.968
Alright.
Wait, that's all I'm gonna make.

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:00.567
I'm gonna go -- That's it.
That's simple.

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:02.667
Is that enough?
[ Cheers ]

00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:04.767
Alright, audience
seems to like --

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:06.801
-Here is mine.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:11.934
If I beat Jacques Pépin at
a sandwich making contest, yes!

00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:14.000
Whoo! I'm excited.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.300
-Can I put that --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.868
-No, whoa, where'd you get that?

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:19.300
-Right there.
-Oh, I love you.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.734
Happy Thanksgiving.
-Thank you.

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:22.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:26.067
-Oh, Tariq,
can you let him know?

00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:27.601
-Take -- Take --
It's time to take the --

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:29.067
-Stop the song.
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:30.634
Wait. Oh, yeah.

00:05:30.634 --> 00:05:31.868
Alright.
-I'm ready?

00:05:31.868 --> 00:05:33.534
-Yeah.

00:05:33.534 --> 00:05:36.000
-Quest.
-Here, I'll take it.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.267
-[ French accent ] We have
two turkey sandwiches here.

00:05:38.267 --> 00:05:39.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.434 --> 00:05:43.601
-Okay.
-One is made by Jacques Pépin.

00:05:43.601 --> 00:05:46.200
[ Normal voice ]
Alright, so take a bite and
let's see what you think.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.167
-Alright.
-Yep. Start with that one.

00:05:50.334 --> 00:05:53.000
Okay, alright.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.400
-Hm.
-Okay.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:56.267
-Turkey's great.
-Yep, it is good.

00:05:56.267 --> 00:05:58.667
Yeah, great. He said "great."

00:05:58.667 --> 00:06:02.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.834
-Someone should hold the tray
for him.

00:06:04.834 --> 00:06:05.868
-Yeah, no, this is getting good.

00:06:05.868 --> 00:06:06.901
-He needs two hands
for that one.

00:06:06.901 --> 00:06:07.968
-Ooh, ooh.

00:06:10.934 --> 00:06:13.434
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.434 --> 00:06:15.601
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

00:06:15.601 --> 00:06:17.367
-There's a lot going on with
this one.

00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:19.501
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.501 --> 00:06:21.634
-Not going down. Not going down.

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:25.667
-Alright. I'll say this much.

00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:27.501
Because he's a better cook
than I am,

00:06:27.501 --> 00:06:30.200
I would have probably made
this sandwich.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.801
So, this is more me,

00:06:31.801 --> 00:06:34.033
but this one actually tastes
a little better.

00:06:34.033 --> 00:06:36.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:36.167 --> 00:06:37.267
Wait. Who won?

00:06:37.267 --> 00:06:39.067
-You guessed correctly.
That's Jacques's.

00:06:39.067 --> 00:06:41.934
That's mine. That's mine.
That's Jacques's.

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:45.167
That's correct.
That's exactly the right choice.

00:06:45.167 --> 00:06:47.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:47.901 --> 00:06:50.334
You're the champ. Jacques Pépin!

00:06:50.334 --> 00:06:51.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:51.767 --> 00:06:55.501
Go to jp.foundation to learn
more about Jacques's

00:06:55.501 --> 00:06:58.300
video series "Cook with Jacques
and Friends."

00:06:58.300 --> 00:06:59.934
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:06:59.934 --> 00:07:01.133
Stick around, everybody.

